---
import Shell from '../layouts/Shell.astro';
import Field from '../components/Field.astro';
import { link } from '../lib/links';
---

<Shell
  title="Illatio — Intelligence, within reach"
  description="Open inference systems, efficient model research, and a planned cloud platform. Illatio builds AI infrastructure around the hardware we have."
>
  <section class="hero wrap">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <div class="eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span> Systems / research / possibility</div><h1>
        Intelligence,<br /><em>within reach.</em>
      </h1><p class="lead">
        Better AI infrastructure starts with making more of what we have. We build open inference
        systems and explore efficient models for a wider world of hardware.
      </p><div class="actions">
        <a class="button" href={link('guild')}>Meet Guild <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a
          class="text-link"
          href="#ecosystem">Explore Illatio <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a
        >
      </div><p class="small-note">Independent. Open by design. Under development.</p>
    </div><Field />
  </section>
  <section id="ecosystem" class="section wrap">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <span class="section-label">01 / Our ecosystem</span><div>
        <h2>One ambition.<br />Three ways forward.</h2><p>
          From the engine on your machine to questions at the edge of model design, our work
          connects practical systems with long-term research.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div><div class="pillars">
      <article class="pillar">
        <span class="number">01</span><span class="status"
          ><span class="dot"></span> Open source · active development</span
        ><h3>Guild</h3><p>
          A native inference engine for Mixture-of-Experts models. Put GPU memory, system RAM, and
          CPU compute to work together.
        </p><a class="text-link" href={link('guild')}
          >Discover the engine <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
        >
      </article><article class="pillar">
        <span class="number">02</span><span class="status">Research initiative</span><h3>
          Guild Labs
        </h3><p>
          Exploring efficient language models, sparse architectures, and ternary representations.
          Home of the proposed Eon family.
        </p><a class="text-link" href={link('labs')}
          >Explore our questions <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
        >
      </article><article class="pillar">
        <span class="number">03</span><span class="status">In development</span><h3>
          Illatio Cloud
        </h3><p>
          Our planned hosted inference platform. Taking the systems thinking behind Guild toward a
          managed experience.
        </p><a class="text-link" href={link('cloud')}
          >See the direction <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
        >
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section wrap">
    <div class="statement">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">02 / A different starting point</span><h2>
          The machine you have.<br /><em>The possibility inside it.</em>
        </h2>
      </div><div>
        <p>
          Useful intelligence should not depend on having the newest accelerator. Sparse models give
          us another path: many parameters, only a fraction of the experts active for each token.
        </p><p>
          Guild turns that observation into systems software. Labs asks how the models themselves
          could become more efficient. Cloud explores how to make those systems easier to access.
        </p><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/guild-inference"
          >Follow the work in the open <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
        >
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section wrap">
    <div class="band">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Start with what exists today</span><h2>
          An engine you can read,<br />build, and run.
        </h2><p>
          Explore Guild’s source-backed documentation, model compatibility, and measured
          performance.
        </p>
      </div><a class="button" href={link('docs')}
        >Start building <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
      >
    </div>
  </section>
</Shell>
